<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese bonds opened with short maturities well supported and 10-year bonds awaiting direction from the U.S. market.</p>
<p>&quot;Shorter bonds look firm but the longer maturities are desperately short of liquidity and are looking to Madrid and New York to set the tone,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Dealers said profit-taking was also blocking a stronger rise in three- and five-year bonds.</p>
<p>The average yield on Portuguese three-month Treasury bills eased to 5.6672 percent from 5.8660 percent previously.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
